":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 48% of normal in October to November and 56% in August to September. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 43% and April to May at 51% on the middle of the grids. Grid 22115 had its driest year in 2007 at 71%.</p>"}
